  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The cut-off voltage of the diodes (shown in figure) in forward bias is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. The current through the resister of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> is _____ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mA</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c75faf00-65b9-40c2-923e-46d06cab17a6-image.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 154px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Here diode&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is forward biased and diode <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is reverse biased.</p><p>So, no current will flow through diode&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;resistor.</p><p>Current through the resistor of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math></p>",
